    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d888">

                <pb facs="0702" n="620" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg620"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the American Ambassador.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-04-17"><hi rendition="#italic">April 17,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your No. 253,
                    of November 18, 1910, transmitting a note<anchor n="1" xml:id="d888-f1"/> from
                    the department of government stating that in future foreigners in Mexican
                    prisons may communicate with the diplomatic and consular officers of their
                    respective countries.</p>
                <p>I inclose for your information a copy of an instruction which the Department has
                    addressed to the minister at Guatemala City<anchor n="2" xml:id="d888-f2"/>
                    requesting him to make representations to the President of Guatemala, with a
                    view to bringing about a similar modification of the system of “incomunicación”
                    which prevails in that country.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d888-f1" n="1" xml:id="d888-f1-content">
                <p>This refers to the communication to the Minister for Foreign Affairs; there was
                    no other inclosure.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d888-f2" n="2" xml:id="d888-f2-content">
                <p>See <ref target="#pg275">page 275</ref>.</p>
            </note>
